quired: To ask (someone) for something; to request.', '📖 causal: 🔹 causal: (grammar) a word (such as because) that expresses a reason or a cause', '📖 questions: 🔹 questions: A sentence, phrase or word which asks for information, reply or response; an interrogative.', '📄 does: Does may refer to:A form of the English verb do\nDeer, a ruminant mammal belonging to the family Cervidae\nplural of John Doe, a number of unnamed individuals\nDoes (album), an album by rock/jazz band The Slip\nDoes (band), a Japanese rock band\n\n', '📄 big: Big or BIG may refer to:Big, of great size or degree', '📄 they: In Modern English, they is a third-person pronoun relating to a grammatical subject.', '📄 type: Type may refer to:', '📄 from: From may refer to:', '📄 property: Property is a system of rights that gives people legal control of valuable things, and also refers to the valuable things themselves. Depending on the nature of the property, an owner of property may have the right to consume, alter, share, rent, sell, exchange, transfer, give away, or destroy it, or to exclude others from doing these things, as well as to perhaps abandon it; whereas regardless of the nature of the property, the owner thereof has the right to properly use it under the granted property rights.', '📄 about: About may refer to:About (surname)\nAbout.com, an online source for original information and advice\nabout.me, a personal web hosting service\nAbout URI scheme, an internal URI scheme\nAbout box, a dialog box that displays information related to a computer software\nAbout equal sign, symbol used to indicate values are approximately equal', "📄 World War: A world war is an international conflict that involves most or all of the world's major powers. Conventionally, the term is reserved for two major international conflicts that occurred during the first half of the 20th century, World War I (1914–1918) and World War II (1939–1945), although some historians have also characterized other global conflicts as 